       Inconsistent use of terminology around the term _s_y_s_t_e_m _a_c_c_o_u_n_t in  docs
       and  code  is  a  bug.   Please report this and allow us to improve our
       docs.

       aadddduusseerr takes special attention to be directly usable in  Debian  main‐
       tainer  scripts  without  conditional  wrappers,  error suppression and
       other scaffolding.  The only thing that the package  maintainer  should
       need  to  code  is  a  check  for the presence of the executable in the
       postrm script.  The aadddduusseerr maintainers consider  the  need  for  addi‐
       tional  scaffolding  a  bug  and  encourage their fellow Debian package
       maintainers to file bugs against the aadddduusseerr package in this case.


